    skos:prefLabel 'wet sieving, acid digestion, stannous chloride reduction'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The sediment sample was separated into size fractions by passing through sieves as a slurry before complete dissolution by aggressive attack with a strong acid followed by reaction (usually to reduce mercury) with stannous chloride.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:S03::S03222'^^xsd:string .
